    <statement><p>Find the vector parametric equations for the line.
in the direction of the vector <m>-4\,\mathit{\vec i}+4\,\mathit{\vec j}-4\,\mathit{\vec k}</m> and
through the point <m>\left(-3,-3,-1\right)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\vec r(t) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-3,-3,-1\right)+\left(-4\,\mathit{\vec i}+4\,\mathit{\vec j}-4\,\mathit{\vec k}\right)t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\vec r(t) = \left(-3+\left(-4\right)t\right)\,\mathit{\vec i}+\left(-3+4t\right)\,\mathit{\vec j}+\left(-1+\left(-4\right)t\right)\,\mathit{\vec k}</me>




</solution>
